.TH GIT-@-REBASE 1 "August 2025" "GitAT v1.1.0" "Git Workflow Management Tool"
.SH NAME
git-@-rebase \- Rebase current branch onto another branch with enhanced options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git @ rebase
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBrebase\fR command rebases the current branch onto another branch with enhanced options and safety features. It provides a user-friendly interface for common rebase operations.
.PP
The command includes safety checks, automatic remote updates, and user confirmation for destructive operations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B onto <branch>
Rebase current branch onto specified branch
.TP
.B interactive, i [commit-range]
Start interactive rebase (default: last 5 commits)
.TP
.B abort
Abort current rebase operation
.TP
.B continue
Continue current rebase operation
.TP
.B skip
Skip current commit in rebase
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
All standard git rebase options are supported and passed through to the underlying git command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Rebase onto trunk branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ rebase
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rebase onto specific branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ rebase onto develop
.fi
.RE
.PP
Interactive rebase of last 3 commits:
.RS
.nf
git @ rebase interactive HEAD~3
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rebase with git options:
.RS
.nf
git @ rebase onto main --autosquash
.fi
.RE
.PP
Abort current rebase:
.RS
.nf
git @ rebase abort
.fi
.RE
.SH FEATURES
.PP
The rebase command includes several features:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Trunk integration with automatic trunk branch detection
.IP \(bu 2
Safety checks to validate that branches exist before rebasing
.IP \(bu 2
Full support for interactive rebasing
.IP \(bu 2
Commands for conflict resolution (abort, continue, skip)
.IP \(bu 2
Automatic pulling of latest changes before rebasing
.IP \(bu 2
User confirmation for destructive operations
.RE
.SH BEST PRACTICES
.PP
When using the rebase command:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Always rebase onto the latest trunk branch before creating PRs
.IP \(bu 2
Use interactive rebase to clean up commit history
.IP \(bu 2
Abort rebase if conflicts are too complex to resolve
.IP \(bu 2
Continue rebase after resolving conflicts
.IP \(bu 2
Skip commits that cause persistent conflicts
.RE
.SH WORKFLOW
.PP
The rebase command follows this workflow:
.IP 1. 4
Detect target branch (automatically or user-specified)
.IP 2. 4
Update target branch with latest changes from remote (if available)
.IP 3. 4
Confirm action with user
.IP 4. 4
Execute rebase with appropriate options
.IP 5. 4
Show results (success or error messages)
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
.BR git-@ (1),
.BR git-@-changelog (1),
.BR git-@-commitizen (1),
.BR git (1)